{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/w9z7cp","slideIndex":1,"text":"The problem is connecting a hazard warning to local context: what affects this location, why it is vulnerable, and how to prepare. Intended early users are students, educators, residents and community volunteers. Official warning services already exist; SACHET provides geo-targeted alerts. Our integration and learning gap is a design hypothesis, not a measured market gap. CEEW's 2025 study assessed 734 districts: about 57% were high or very high heat risk and those districts housed 76% of India's population. These are different denominators and are not counts of our users. 43% is the rounded complement. Sources: https://www.ceew.in/publications/mapping-climate-risks-and-impacts-of-extreme-heatwave-disaster-in-indian-districts; https://sachet.ndma.gov.in/ . Canva chart design: https://canva.link/cbyvxudo1ymblax. The native PowerPoint chart preserves exact rounded data and proportional scaling."}
