{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/9wz610bm","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":64,"top":641,"width":1145,"height":27},"text":"Input: location + feeds + reports     Process: normalization + rules     Output: map + learning + demo status","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":16,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#596A70","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/0xg9rl","slideIndex":3,"text":"Input: selected location, static profiles, external hazard responses, and demo incident reports. Processing: Node.js middleware inside the Vite development server normalizes XML/GeoJSON/CSV, caches feeds and assigns coordinates to states with point-in-polygon logic. A finite-state workflow constrains incident actions. Output: React screens and Cesium map markers. Static profiles are bundled with the frontend. Incidents and audit entries are in memory; there is no persistent database. The optional chatbot uses a configured external LLM API; no disaster-prediction model is trained. The AI does not dispatch teams or independently verify current hazards. Source: vite.config.js; server/hazards.js; server/incidents.js; server/chat.js; src/components/IndiaGlobe.jsx. Main active map engine is CesiumJS."}
