{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/lhctrz","slideIndex":5,"text":"A classroom demonstration runs on a laptop with Node.js, browser and internet. React, Vite and CesiumJS provide the application foundation. Public data services may have terms, quotas or key requirements; FIRMS requires a key and chatbot use may incur provider charges. Free or low-cost access does not imply unlimited production usage. Cache intervals reduce repeat requests: USGS 1 min, official alerts 2 min, Open-Meteo 5 min, FIRMS 15 min. They are not end-to-end warning latency guarantees. Public scaling requires a separate production backend, authentication, persistent storage, quotas and monitoring. No load testing is claimed. Source: package.json; server/hazards.js; docs/LIVE_OPERATIONS.md; docs/CHATBOT_SETUP.md. Canva chart design: https://canva.link/cbyvxudo1ymblax; native chart recreated for exact proportional data."}
