{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/aw0n3i","slideIndex":6,"text":"Expected benefits: clearer local risk understanding for students and residents; structured practice for community volunteers; a basis for feedback from educators and domain reviewers. These benefits have not been measured in a field study. Current software evidence: five bundled location profiles, four integrated hazard/feed families and 19 passing automated tests reported in the repository review on 8 October 2026, with mocked providers and simulated incidents. Tests do not establish scientific accuracy or real-world safety. Proposed pilot: compare time to locate a relevant source, a short before/after knowledge quiz, and completion of a simulated incident lifecycle. Collect baseline values before estimating improvements. Source: supplied ClimateGuard_AI_Resilience_Blueprint.pptx, slides 14–18. These slides describe a concept, not proof of validated operational performance. Source: locationsData.js; hazards.js; npm test results from project review."}
